From 5d1440767763f94213d1edc1b24ed803f0b215fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: News_92 <almazpro0927@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:21:17 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign IQ test result screen: rings, history, share card

- Score and level badge become large and emotional (animated count-up,
  dynamic teacher line by percent threshold).
- Replace the three flat easy/medium/hard cards with a concentric
  activity-ring SVG chart (colored by per-category threshold) plus a
  compact legend.
- Add a comparison row (top-15% chip, vs. average) and a 5-attempt
  history sparkline built from the existing iqResults store.
- Add an AI-teacher "what's next" tip driven by weak-category
  thresholds, linking to the trainer's weak-topics filter.
- Add a "Share result" flow: a 1080x1080 canvas card (gradient, score,
  level, name, date, QR with graceful no-network/CORS fallback) opened
  through the site's existing Sky.modal(), with download / Telegram /
  VK / copy-text actions and Web Share API where supported.
- All new strings run through the existing Sky.t/Sky.L i18n system
  (RU/EN); all new colors use the sky.css design tokens already
  defined in the codebase (--ok/--warn/--no/--m-learn/--panel/--line).

Verified end-to-end with a headless-browser run of the real quiz flow
(multiple attempts, history sparkline, share modal, RU and EN).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfqGV45jVWTSPWXZN8du
